  "note": [
    "The table the Palestinian Arabic number composer is held to.",
    "Every row is a number a speaker would recognise, written out in full,",
    "against a lexicon written the way a teacher would write it.",
    "",
    "Where the words came from: every spelling in `system` below, and every",
    "row NOT marked `check`, is the wording this app has shipped since 0.152",
    "— it was the data of tests/numbers.test.mjs, which was written with the",
    "feature and has been in front of learners since. Those are as verified",
    "as anything in the repository.",
    "",
    "A row marked `check` is a HYPOTHESIS this plan introduced and nobody",
    "has confirmed. They are the rows to read first, and they are all of one",
    "of three kinds:",
    "  - the form a numeral takes directly before a noun (`construct`), which",
    "    this app never asked a teacher for before;",
    "  - whether ten thousand takes that form too;",
    "  - whether the unit inside 21-99 agrees with a feminine noun, which",
    "    the written language says it does and this composer does not do.",
    "Strike any of them out and the fix is either a different word in the",
    "box or an override; neither is a change to the composer.",
    "",
    "`reviewedBy` and `reviewedOn` are empty on purpose. They are filled in",
    "by whoever checks this, and a blank pair is the honest statement that",
    "the `check` rows are still guesses."
  ],
